WEBVTT

00:27.902 --> 00:32.615
"You must be the change
you wish to see in the world."

00:33.742 --> 00:35.243
That's what Gandhi said.

00:37.662 --> 00:38.663
I…

00:40.749 --> 00:42.792
will create a utopia here.

00:45.420 --> 00:48.173
For those who have fallen into despair…

00:51.843 --> 00:53.344
if we don't have hope,

00:54.137 --> 00:55.555
we just need to make it!

00:59.350 --> 01:01.186
This will be the land of hope.

01:03.813 --> 01:07.776
I will make this place the second Beach!

02:35.530 --> 02:39.450
BEACH

03:16.196 --> 03:17.947
How long are you going to sleep?

03:21.659 --> 03:22.869
Did you drink too much?

03:32.587 --> 03:34.088
Did you get any information?

03:35.465 --> 03:36.716
Not at all.

03:41.012 --> 03:43.014
I should go gather some information now.

03:46.726 --> 03:48.895
It seems like Hatter
has taken a liking to you.

03:50.271 --> 03:53.066
The militants have their eye on you,
so be careful.

03:54.442 --> 03:56.361
You don't know what they'll do to you.

04:03.910 --> 04:07.622
I heard this from the guys who drove
all the way to the suburbs.

04:07.705 --> 04:11.668
The further you get from the city,
the more run-down the streets are,

04:11.751 --> 04:14.128
and beyond that,
it looks like a jungle of sorts.

04:14.629 --> 04:17.382
And they didn't proceed further than that.

04:17.465 --> 04:18.508
Seriously?

04:18.591 --> 04:22.637
I heard that game arenas
are only within Tokyo!

04:22.720 --> 04:25.515
Let's pump it up until the end!

04:26.975 --> 04:29.769
There are rumors of those who tried
escaping from the country via a boat,

04:29.852 --> 04:32.230
but those lasers from the sky

04:32.313 --> 04:33.856
killed all of them.

04:33.940 --> 04:34.857
Have you heard of that?

04:34.941 --> 04:41.155
So does that mean only people
in Tokyo disappeared?

04:41.239 --> 04:43.408
But if this only happened in Tokyo,

04:43.491 --> 04:45.576
the SDF would have come
to our rescue, right?

04:46.160 --> 04:50.498
The fact that they didn't come means
everyone in Japan disappeared, right?

04:50.581 --> 04:52.083
Even the U.S. army didn't come for us.

04:52.583 --> 04:56.129
Don't tell me…
everyone in the entire world disappeared?

04:58.047 --> 05:02.093
Aliens inserted a chip into our brains
and are toying with us.

05:02.635 --> 05:05.430
I'm sure no one would be able
to escape from this place.

05:05.513 --> 05:06.389
Let me drink some.

05:11.102 --> 05:13.313
The more I hear,
the more depressing it gets.

05:14.856 --> 05:15.982
Perhaps…

05:16.858 --> 05:19.027
our only hope really lies
in the playing cards.

05:28.411 --> 05:31.456
I'll head to the annex basement now.

05:33.541 --> 05:34.500
Don't overdo it.

05:35.543 --> 05:37.837
I'll go get food supplies
and any weapons that we can use.

05:37.920 --> 05:40.048
I'll also gather some information
in case we need it.

05:46.304 --> 05:48.264
"In case we need it?" What does she mean?

05:56.689 --> 05:58.566
Hey, can I ask both of you something?

06:01.319 --> 06:03.112
Wait, I'm not trying to hit on you!

07:13.141 --> 07:15.560
That is the true nature
of this utopia.

07:19.355 --> 07:20.940
This is part of Beach's rule.

07:21.691 --> 07:23.401
"Death to the traitors."

07:38.749 --> 07:39.625
Arisu.

07:41.127 --> 07:44.505
You and Usagi seem to have collected
a vast amount of information.

07:45.381 --> 07:46.716
What are you both planning?

07:49.427 --> 07:50.553
Nothing much.

07:54.974 --> 07:56.767
I'll cut to the chase.

07:58.186 --> 08:00.980
How will you live in this world
that's full of despair?

08:02.607 --> 08:03.649
"How"?

08:15.495 --> 08:17.497
I just want to know
the answers to my questions.

08:19.332 --> 08:21.459
The ones behind this crazy game.

08:23.920 --> 08:26.547
And who killed Karube and Chota.

08:32.178 --> 08:33.930
I thought I'd be able to survive

08:34.764 --> 08:37.225
and return to the original world
with everyone.

08:40.228 --> 08:41.854
If that is not possible,

08:43.022 --> 08:45.566
I want Usagi to return, at the very least.

08:47.693 --> 08:49.654
This is the only reason
why I'm still alive.

08:53.157 --> 08:54.283
What a tearjerker.

08:57.954 --> 08:59.121
Your dream…

09:00.498 --> 09:02.083
It's cool,

09:04.210 --> 09:06.295
but it's not practical at all.

09:08.589 --> 09:13.594
You'll have to win all the games
and become the next Number One,

09:14.220 --> 09:15.304
but that's impossible.

09:16.472 --> 09:18.224
It has nothing to do with you guys.

09:18.766 --> 09:20.768
We think that you have potential.

09:22.520 --> 09:25.481
- What?
- That's why we came to meet you.

09:27.608 --> 09:28.776
What do you mean?

09:31.320 --> 09:34.198
What if I said there's a way to change
the status quo all at once?

09:41.289 --> 09:44.000
We're off to the game arena!

09:49.714 --> 09:51.966
They gathered quite a number of firearms.

09:52.717 --> 09:56.345
It was kept in the deepest room
in the annex, and there were patrols too.

09:57.722 --> 09:59.682
As long as they have those firearms,

09:59.765 --> 10:02.143
Hatter will be
in an advantageous position.

10:08.774 --> 10:09.609
What's the matter?

10:17.825 --> 10:19.160
I'm off!

10:23.831 --> 10:27.960
Hatter is trying to keep
the militants in check,

10:28.836 --> 10:30.838
but it's only a matter of time
before they retaliate.

10:32.965 --> 10:36.093
If that happens, this place will be
controlled by the militants

10:36.177 --> 10:38.179
who don't know how to use their brains.

10:38.763 --> 10:40.264
Then there'd be no point staying here.

10:42.183 --> 10:43.726
What are you planning?

10:46.812 --> 10:48.898
I'm planning
to steal all the playing cards

10:50.691 --> 10:52.068
and leave the Beach.

11:03.162 --> 11:04.205
The Beach.

11:05.956 --> 11:07.917
A utopia built upon charisma.

11:11.587 --> 11:12.421
However,

11:13.756 --> 11:16.425
maybe that's just our imagination.

11:16.509 --> 11:17.927
BEACH

11:19.470 --> 11:21.263
A utopia doesn't exist in this world.

11:23.516 --> 11:24.392
Usagi.

11:26.811 --> 11:28.896
I'd like to talk to you about something.

11:35.403 --> 11:38.656
KABUKICHO

11:38.739 --> 11:40.074
THIS WAY TO THE GAME ARENA

11:55.798 --> 11:56.757
This way.

12:02.555 --> 12:03.848
Kabukicho, huh?

12:05.766 --> 12:06.934
This takes me back.

12:19.739 --> 12:23.242
BEACH

12:23.325 --> 12:24.744
I can't wait.

12:24.827 --> 12:26.454
- Hey!
- Excuse me, sorry!

12:41.218 --> 12:43.721
Where the hell is the GPS chip?

12:48.684 --> 12:52.146
- So you really were here!
- Hey, don't come in without my permission!

12:55.608 --> 13:00.654
Well, something bad happened.
Please come with me!

13:01.489 --> 13:02.406
Hurry!

13:09.079 --> 13:10.915
Hey, wait up.

13:10.998 --> 13:12.625
Where did you guys come from?

13:13.125 --> 13:14.794
We didn't ask you guys to come here!

13:15.961 --> 13:18.255
I called him over.

13:20.341 --> 13:22.676
Hey, don't go gathering people
on your own.

13:23.677 --> 13:26.013
There's something important
he has to hear.

13:27.681 --> 13:28.516
Let's go in.

13:31.519 --> 13:32.353
See you later.

13:39.318 --> 13:40.569
What happened?

13:41.278 --> 13:42.321
Who knows?

13:43.322 --> 13:45.074
It must be something serious.

14:28.742 --> 14:30.411
It seems like he couldn't clear the game.

14:31.203 --> 14:34.081
The maintenance team
found him by chance in Shinjuku

14:34.164 --> 14:35.958
while we were refilling gasoline.

14:39.753 --> 14:42.464
Hey, don't touch him as you please.

14:42.548 --> 14:44.133
You dissection maniac.

14:49.179 --> 14:50.723
He was shot by a gun.

14:51.473 --> 14:54.226
Did his game involve guns?

14:54.894 --> 14:58.772
Most likely. Some of those
near the game area heard gunshots too.

14:59.356 --> 15:03.611
Oh, my. He should have brought
the militants along with him!

15:15.039 --> 15:17.625
What's going to happen to the Beach?

15:19.251 --> 15:23.547
Keep this a secret from the rest.
They'll be shaken by this.

15:25.716 --> 15:28.052
I'll be the next leader
since I'm Number two.

15:28.636 --> 15:30.012
Wait a second.

15:31.680 --> 15:34.475
Shouldn't the strongest person
be the leader?

15:35.851 --> 15:39.521
We're the ones who have been
getting rid of the traitors,

15:40.105 --> 15:42.816
yet we've been treated
as shadows the entire time.

15:42.900 --> 15:44.902
This unfair treatment ends today!

15:44.985 --> 15:46.779
If Number One dies,

15:46.862 --> 15:49.365
everyone moves up by a number.
We agreed on this rule.

15:50.366 --> 15:53.285
The snobbish dictator is dead.

15:53.369 --> 15:55.371
The power has shifted, hasn't it?

15:56.747 --> 15:59.750
Let's just be democratic
and go with the majority.

16:01.919 --> 16:05.381
Who agrees that Aguni
should be the new leader?

16:15.849 --> 16:17.935
What a bad reaction.

16:19.436 --> 16:20.437
Last Boss.

16:38.163 --> 16:39.790
I'll ask again.

16:40.499 --> 16:42.710
Who agrees that Aguni
should be the new leader?

16:56.640 --> 16:57.558
This…

16:58.267 --> 17:00.019
is not a majority rule.

17:01.103 --> 17:03.522
It is, isn't it?

17:05.024 --> 17:07.359
You're free to vote after all.

17:17.411 --> 17:20.456
What about the former Number Two
over there?

17:21.206 --> 17:22.166
What will you do?

17:33.469 --> 17:34.678
What about you?

17:41.060 --> 17:44.688
Are you looking down on us, Chishiya?

17:45.314 --> 17:46.774
But you guys really are stupid.

17:50.569 --> 17:53.197
Those eyes of yours really piss me off.

17:54.281 --> 17:56.867
It's so condescending.

18:03.082 --> 18:05.042
I vote for Aguni to be the leader.

18:06.835 --> 18:09.296
Are you all right with losing me
as a precious "yes" vote?

18:12.841 --> 18:16.136
Well, I hope you reflect on
how you should act in the future.

18:18.430 --> 18:21.225
Hey, what are you spacing out for?

18:22.559 --> 18:25.270
Were you never taught
that you should reply to people?

18:26.396 --> 18:28.190
Whose side are you on?

18:31.401 --> 18:33.362
You were really scared
for a moment there, right?

18:34.863 --> 18:36.031
That's so funny!

18:38.158 --> 18:39.576
All right.

18:40.744 --> 18:45.290
Suddenly everyone's voting "yes."
So the new leader is decided, right?

18:45.374 --> 18:47.459
Hatter would not allow this.

18:48.752 --> 18:51.171
If he were alive,
he would not have allowed this.

18:53.799 --> 18:55.717
But he's dead.

18:57.886 --> 19:02.391
The dead won't know what's going on.

19:04.935 --> 19:07.229
See?

19:10.649 --> 19:11.775
Enough.

19:18.699 --> 19:20.159
From today onwards,

19:21.577 --> 19:23.287
I will be the Beach's new king.

19:26.290 --> 19:28.333
Isn't this wonderful?

19:33.797 --> 19:37.134
Now, boss.
What's left is the succession ceremony.

19:37.676 --> 19:40.304
Let's open the black envelope.

19:50.814 --> 19:52.357
The black envelope.

19:53.567 --> 19:56.153
The poker cards gathered
by all the members of Beach

19:56.904 --> 20:00.657
are kept in the safe
in Hatter's royal suite room.

20:01.950 --> 20:04.578
The passcode to the safe

20:05.204 --> 20:09.374
is kept and sealed
inside the black envelope.

20:11.084 --> 20:15.547
The envelope is opaque
and kept in utmost secrecy,

20:16.340 --> 20:20.802
and can be opened
only when there is a new Number One.

20:26.183 --> 20:29.353
The new Number One
will check the passcode alone

20:29.937 --> 20:32.147
in front of all the executive members.

20:42.616 --> 20:45.702
Then, he will place the paper
with the passcode written on it

20:45.786 --> 20:49.206
into a new envelope and seal it again.

20:49.957 --> 20:50.832
It will then be signed

20:50.916 --> 20:53.043
by all executive members
before it's stashed away again.

21:03.262 --> 21:05.889
First, Arisu will infiltrate
the royal suite.

21:06.556 --> 21:08.267
Then he will search for the safe

21:08.350 --> 21:10.644
and steal all the playing cards inside.

21:12.854 --> 21:15.440
- What about the passcode?
- I have an idea of that.

21:17.067 --> 21:19.152
I'll tell you
when you're in front of the safe.

21:21.947 --> 21:23.115
You're really cautious.

21:24.491 --> 21:25.575
I got it.

21:27.452 --> 21:29.746
Usagi and Kuina will be on the lookout.

21:30.789 --> 21:34.334
This is too dangerous.
If we're discovered, we'll be killed.

21:39.381 --> 21:41.800
This is the only way
to change the current situation.

21:43.719 --> 21:47.556
Now that Hatter is dead
and there's no unity at the Beach,

21:47.639 --> 21:49.349
the time is right for this plan.

22:03.864 --> 22:05.907
The leader has changed.

22:08.785 --> 22:10.662
Hatter is no longer with us.

22:11.413 --> 22:15.584
The new leader will be Aguni.

22:19.838 --> 22:21.298
How noisy. Shut up!

22:23.633 --> 22:28.055
It appears that Hatter failed
in his game and couldn't return.

22:29.264 --> 22:32.267
Through majority vote
among the executive members,

22:33.060 --> 22:35.395
it's been decided
that Aguni will be the new Number One.

22:37.898 --> 22:40.609
Now, let's hear from Aguni.

22:41.485 --> 22:44.196
You guys better listen properly.

22:52.746 --> 22:53.580
Now,

22:54.373 --> 22:56.416
what Niragi said is everything.

22:58.085 --> 23:00.545
The new leader is making a speech
in the lobby.

23:02.756 --> 23:08.053
All executive members
and the militants are at the annex.

23:08.804 --> 23:10.680
We won't get another chance like this.

23:13.683 --> 23:16.395
I'll let you guys know
if there are any changes.

23:16.478 --> 23:18.647
I'm counting on you, Arisu.

23:20.941 --> 23:21.942
Understood.

23:27.280 --> 23:29.741
With Hatter gone
as the previous Number One,

23:30.617 --> 23:33.370
I now have full control over the Beach.

23:33.870 --> 23:37.082
Follow my orders, live for me,

23:38.917 --> 23:40.544
and die for me.

23:54.933 --> 23:56.017
I found it.

23:57.561 --> 23:59.104
So, what's the passcode?

23:59.187 --> 24:00.814
It's 8022.

24:01.314 --> 24:03.233
Did you see the contents of the letter?

24:03.775 --> 24:04.818
No.

24:05.444 --> 24:08.029
But Aguni's expression told me everything.

24:09.322 --> 24:10.657
That instant,

24:11.158 --> 24:13.243
Aguni's face looked dark.

24:14.536 --> 24:16.496
It was as if he was surprised

24:17.247 --> 24:19.291
and perplexed.

24:21.543 --> 24:23.628
I'm sure the contents must be empty.

24:24.463 --> 24:26.715
Empty? Then what about
the passcode you told me?

24:29.217 --> 24:30.760
The wax seal.

24:32.012 --> 24:35.348
It was embossed with the Boss' ring,
and it formed numbers.

24:36.808 --> 24:38.602
That was the code itself.

24:39.561 --> 24:41.062
It's 8022.

24:44.524 --> 24:46.610
I wouldn't want to be your enemy.

24:57.287 --> 24:58.455
It won't open!

25:01.166 --> 25:02.209
Chishiya!

25:04.336 --> 25:05.795
Hey! Chishiya!

25:08.340 --> 25:11.301
You really came in so brazenly.

25:19.017 --> 25:21.269
- Why?
- Let me go!

25:21.770 --> 25:24.439
- Stay still!
- Usagi!

25:25.649 --> 25:26.650
Arisu!

25:27.150 --> 25:29.945
Stop shouting for Usagi, you idiot!

25:30.445 --> 25:31.279
Arisu!

25:35.367 --> 25:37.452
You saved me, Chishiya.

25:37.994 --> 25:39.746
We caught them
thanks to your perceptiveness.

25:40.330 --> 25:42.707
No problem. It was what I should do.

25:44.209 --> 25:46.545
Let go! Arisu!

25:54.010 --> 25:55.095
Arisu!

25:58.598 --> 25:59.641
What?

25:59.724 --> 26:00.642
Oh, my.

26:02.102 --> 26:03.812
Are you sleepy already?

26:08.608 --> 26:10.902
Bring him to that room!

26:28.837 --> 26:32.632
I heard that your visa expires tomorrow.

26:36.219 --> 26:41.141
You'll have no hearing, no sight,
and no clue what the time is.

26:41.766 --> 26:47.439
I can't imagine the fear as you wait
for the laser to shoot through your head!

26:49.524 --> 26:51.610
In the meantime,

26:52.193 --> 26:56.781
we'll enjoy the best of our time
with your dear Usagi!

26:59.659 --> 27:01.077
Bye!

28:01.596 --> 28:03.765
How are things on your side, Kuina?

28:05.517 --> 28:08.645
Aguni is still in his room.

28:10.689 --> 28:12.565
I'm so bored now.

28:13.900 --> 28:16.945
Then, shall we proceed with our plan?

28:19.364 --> 28:22.033
I don't know if Arisu is clever or stupid.

28:22.659 --> 28:25.412
There's no way the cards
would be kept in an ordinary safe.

28:26.955 --> 28:29.541
Then where is the real safe?

28:30.917 --> 28:33.545
When Arisu found the fake safe,

28:34.546 --> 28:36.881
Aguni, who usually does not waver,

28:37.465 --> 28:39.008
was looking toward a certain location.

28:42.971 --> 28:46.307
I believe
that the contents of the envelope

28:46.891 --> 28:49.477
did not contain a passcode
or an empty letter…

28:53.273 --> 28:56.609
but instead, it might have been a drawing.

29:19.883 --> 29:20.759
Found it.

29:21.718 --> 29:23.386
So you used him for this?

29:25.221 --> 29:28.808
To gain something,
you need to lose something.

29:29.976 --> 29:32.979
He's just a sacrifice.
Things like this happen often, don't they?

29:33.938 --> 29:36.441
No, not at all.

29:37.525 --> 29:40.862
I really don't want to be your enemy.

29:42.280 --> 29:43.615
People often tell me that.

30:48.429 --> 30:50.348
- Let me go!
- You're too noisy!

30:50.431 --> 30:51.266
Hurry up!

30:51.349 --> 30:52.517
- Stop struggling.
- Let go!

30:52.600 --> 30:54.185
- Heave-ho.
- Heave-ho. There you go!

30:57.522 --> 30:59.274
- Stop moving.
- Let go of me!

31:28.928 --> 31:35.602
Rape, assault, fraud, arson, murder…

31:36.644 --> 31:39.314
Why do you think these crimes
are punishable by law?

31:46.404 --> 31:49.240
Why is it that they are prohibited by law?

31:54.287 --> 31:56.289
That's because they are part
of human nature.

32:00.251 --> 32:01.377
Left to our own devices,

32:01.461 --> 32:03.755
humans will rape,
steal, and kill each other.

32:07.342 --> 32:09.010
That's just who we really are.

32:20.647 --> 32:23.066
But there are no laws here.

32:24.525 --> 32:27.111
Isn't it a waste
to not do all these things?

32:28.112 --> 32:32.450
Such human nature empowers us!

33:01.312 --> 33:03.022
Stop fucking around.

33:05.984 --> 33:08.528
The fun is just beginning.

33:32.802 --> 33:34.846
I guess it's time
to say goodbye to this, too.

33:36.139 --> 33:40.143
Don't you feel sorry for him?
Arisu, I mean.

33:41.769 --> 33:42.687
Feel sorry?

33:43.896 --> 33:44.731
Yes.

33:45.523 --> 33:47.191
I feel really sorry for him.

33:51.529 --> 33:54.198
Is there anything
we can't do in order to survive?

34:00.246 --> 34:03.666
If you're so worried,
then you should help him, Kuina.

34:15.219 --> 34:16.095
Don't tell me…

34:19.265 --> 34:20.141
Stop right there!

34:39.077 --> 34:40.036
Seriously?

35:04.060 --> 35:09.398
Thank you for staying
at Seaside Paradise Tokyo.

35:10.483 --> 35:12.860
As a token of our appreciation,

35:12.944 --> 35:18.032
we will now commence a game
for all the guests in the hotel.

35:18.116 --> 35:20.118
ONE PER PERSON

35:21.911 --> 35:24.539
THE GAME WILL NOW COMMENCE

35:29.710 --> 35:30.837
The Beach

35:31.838 --> 35:33.131
is a game arena?

35:33.714 --> 35:34.632
Difficulty,

35:35.633 --> 35:37.093
Ten of Hearts.

35:39.762 --> 35:42.807
- "Ten of Hearts"!
- It finally appeared.

35:46.519 --> 35:50.189
We will now be explaining the rules.

35:50.690 --> 35:53.985
All players are to assemble in the lobby.

35:55.987 --> 36:01.284
I repeat. All players
are to assemble in the lobby.

36:26.100 --> 36:27.685
- Let's go!
- Hurry up!

36:27.768 --> 36:29.937
- Quick!
- What game is it?

36:34.108 --> 36:35.109
Hey!

37:15.942 --> 37:17.026
Momoka!

37:18.444 --> 37:19.570
Momoka!

37:20.154 --> 37:21.405
Why…

37:27.912 --> 37:30.706
Game, "Witch Hunt."

37:32.083 --> 37:35.086
The evil witch who took the girl's life

37:35.169 --> 37:37.255
is hiding among you.

